WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.959 --> 00:00:02.502
People think they know my story,

00:00:02.794 --> 00:00:04.004
but this is our story.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.507
I just need a second, coach.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:08.258
You're on the team here?

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.301
Nah, but I could be if you're lucky.

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:11.261
Me and my boys,

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:12.429
we were balling with each other

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:13.596
since we was like ten.

00:00:13.596 --> 00:00:15.015
Call ourselves the "Fab Four."

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.099
That's going in!

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:16.599
Get up!

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.018
Hey! Hey!

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:20.937
We can win you a state championship.

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:21.938
Guaranteed.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:28.737
When they were young,

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:30.447
I was just trying to find good kids

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:31.823
and they all kinda balanced each other out.

00:00:31.823 --> 00:00:32.615
Willie.

00:00:32.615 --> 00:00:34.200
Both his parents: addicts.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.744
His big brother took him in,

00:00:35.744 --> 00:00:37.120
saved his little brother's life.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.663
Sian, we just wanted Sian

00:00:38.663 --> 00:00:40.331
to work off a little bit of his baby fat.

00:00:40.331 --> 00:00:41.499
Drew was born with

00:00:41.499 --> 00:00:43.209
basketball in his blood.

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:45.378
I picked LeBron

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.713
because he had skills

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.298
and he was a good kid.

00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:49.340
His mom just wants a spot

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.341
where he can be safe

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:51.468
and not get in any trouble.

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:53.386
Come on, pose Denzel!

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.305
We value all the talent

00:00:55.305 --> 00:00:56.931
 you boys are gonna bring to this school.

00:00:56.931 --> 00:00:58.183
Oh my goodness!

00:00:58.183 --> 00:00:58.975
Look at y'all!

00:00:58.975 --> 00:00:59.851
And now tell me,

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.936
which one of y'all is supposed to be Carlton?

00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:02.979
You? You?

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:03.730
Ma, stop!

00:01:07.108 --> 00:01:07.942
They're not very good.

00:01:07.942 --> 00:01:08.568
Now let's try this.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:09.569
You're in the game, let's go.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.491
We may be seeing the beginnings

00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:16.284
of something special here in Akron.

00:01:17.118 --> 00:01:18.286
Yo, watch out!

00:01:18.286 --> 00:01:19.204
You watch out.

00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:20.497
Maybe you'll see some new faces.

00:01:20.497 --> 00:01:21.956
This is Mr. Travis.

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:23.958
Travis slams!

00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:25.502
They're so damn good and they know it.

00:01:25.502 --> 00:01:26.878
We in business!

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:29.714
Just make sure that doesn't tear them apart.

00:01:29.714 --> 00:01:30.381
What's it like coaching

00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:31.925
the best high school player in the country?

00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:34.427
Play some defense.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.763
Sorry, we can't all be the chosen one!

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.514
What'd you say to me?

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:38.932
How successful you become

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.308
depends on how well you

00:01:40.308 --> 00:01:41.893
manage the pressure.

00:01:43.353 --> 00:01:44.479
He's not just your player,

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:45.563
he's your son too.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:46.648
So we just ain't gonna talk

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:47.899
to each other for the whole season?

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.195
What happens if nobody wants me?

00:01:52.195 --> 00:01:53.822
You're a whole lot more than just basketball.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.784
I wanted to make great players out of you.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.537
Your dad wants to make great men.

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:01.830
That'll last a lot longer.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:03.748
We here,

00:02:03.748 --> 00:02:05.208
cause we know what we capable of.

00:02:07.252 --> 00:02:09.379
When you look back at this time in your lives,

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:10.255
it won't be the stats.

00:02:11.756 --> 00:02:13.299
It'll be that person next to you.

00:02:15.927 --> 00:02:17.637
Did you make the time you had together count?

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.766
Right now I'm not thinking about the future.

00:02:21.766 --> 00:02:22.934
I'm thinking about my brothers.

